{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: Room A fixed-next-prefix capacity fallback, head 1d7495bd6a1405a693214b7a2bf9087acae759cf, tree 4f8f4e61d1d5910861d8889a29f81dfc5449709c, branch builder/room-a-fixed-prefix-20261025 (six commits directly on Main f5a6338c, 10 paths, all 10 named by the artifacts). Review request bfdb3ec8, checker promise 1688500c, implementation request f6ba323d (builder promise a2b586e5, parent 1aedd35b; design accepted by the planner in c4a6fc58).\n\nRead order: the primary note at the head in full; the review request, the implementation request and the planner's acceptance; the production diff (archive-driver.ts, archive-adaptive.ts, archive-build.ts, the new archive-finish-cost.ts and archive-fixed-layout.ts, archive-row.ts); the two test files; the seal map; then the surrounding code at the head: ArchiveBudget canSpend/capacityRefusal/spend, the adaptive loop and its refusal handling, the driver's refusal branch, ArchiveRows wake writes (save, defer, prepareCapacityDeferral, clearWake, signal), and the scout's layout bound.\n\nHead and gate. The head differs from the gated checkpoint 64da4edc (tree 1daf599e) only in the primary note (+14/-2: the gate outcome and the remaining-work sentence). Production, tests and seal map are those of the gated checkpoint, so the documents-only follow-up rule applies and no second gate is owed.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The driver selects the fixed strategy before planning spends anything, and only when production wiring, a previous genuine capacity deferral (the validated wake count, used as a mode signal only), a published confirmed v2 row and a frontier base are all present. It reads exactly confirmed+1 by a charged SQL read with a digest check and refuses positions beyond the current head or a hash differing at the head. Initial, conversion, unpublished-anchor and pending-Mark paths keep their code. planRootFixedPublishedArchivePass begins a fresh preparation, runs one complete native inventory, keeps the module-owned result through layout, quote and build (ownedPassManifest/buildOwnedPass are a pure split of the existing function, no second read), rebinds the pin and reviewed policy after the parent-edge await, and quotes the remainder with the same forecastArchiveFinish the adaptive scout uses (moved verbatim into archive-finish-cost.ts). Passing zero for setup and inventory is correct: in the adaptive quote those two terms forecast the final inventory, which in the fixed path has already run and been charged in used; every later read, publication, journal, transfer, bookkeeping and frontier term stays in the quote. Admission is canSpend(R + 65,536 metadata) against the original allowance, that is U + R + 65,536 \u003c= limit on metadata and U + R \u003c= limit on the other five axes; a refusal goes through the existing prepaid capacity wake with site finish-affordability and the 65,536 reserve shown. ArchiveRows' save rewrites the wake without capacityDeferrals, so a confirmation returns the next pass to adaptive batching; defer() keeps the count, so a transient source retry stays on the fixed path (the driver test covers both).\n\nSecurity: no new authority. The count selects a strategy and admits nothing. Target, sources and prepare(next) run fresh on the pass's own budget; inventory, privacy, foreign-source pins and coverage checks are the existing ones; the pin and reviewed policy are re-read after the await and a change refuses as mismatch. No bound, price, deadline, Mark or frontier comparison changes, and no durable state is added (the diagnostic gains a numeric fixedFinish that grants nothing). The seals for archive-build.ts (e144eecf…), archive-driver.ts (7e7a41de…) and archive-row.ts (e96224d4…) reproduce from the maintained producer (sourceSeal in scripts/security-entry-points.mjs) at the head in my run, and scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs passes 4 of 4 at the head (1.31 s).\n\nSimplification: acceptable, with one note. Extracting forecastArchiveFinish and archiveParentMetadata removes the risk of two diverging finish quotes. archiveFixedLayout copies the scout's escaped-JSON upper bound (jsonUpper, same 32/64 prices as ArchiveScoutLayout's private #jsonUpper; archive-plan-fence.ts has a third variant); one shared helper would keep the prices from drifting. Nonblocking.\n\nEvidence, verified by me:\n- Gate 73297: raw result exitCode 0 with expectedHead 64da4edc and expectedTree 1daf599e; gate.stdout shows eight stages at exit 0, \"Tests 3585 passed | 3 skipped (3588)\", Node 42 and Counting 55; stderr empty; install skipped against the lockfile. All 28 files in the evidence manifest match their SHA-256 digests. before.json and after.json differ only in the Vitest results.json cache (size and digest) and the Vite temp directory timestamps, the named cache exceptions. The audit manifest digest is 6d0a268f…, as cited in the builder's acceptance d8732928. The three \"Cannot perform I/O on behalf of a different Durable Object\" log lines also appear three times in the 24 October archive-capacity gates; they are not new.\n- Negative control 26505: fault.patch replaces only the fixed selection with false; vitest.json records 18 passed and 1 failed, the failure in \"adaptive Native passes reserve writing, incremental sending and confirmation before more lookahead\", where the old adaptive route refuses at plan with fixedFinish null. I read the records; I did not rerun it.\n- The driver witness pairs the boundary: a 512 KiB cap refuses with a metadata shortfall; a cap of U + R + 32,768 refuses on the margin alone (R fits); a later full allowance confirms exactly 63 to 64 with every axis of the actual cost at or below used + remaining and at least 65,536 bytes of metadata headroom. The installed Grow witness forces a genuine scout-open capacity retry, then confirms exactly 146 to 147 under the same per-axis checks, then a normal pass drains 148 to 152 with fixedFinish null. The figures in the note (quote 830,681 vs actual 648,076; quote 2,930,245 vs actual 2,633,486, headroom 1,560,818) are the builder's measurements from these runs; I did not rerun them.\n- The failed first installed run 75547 (wrong uses \u003e 0 fixture assumption) stays recorded as a failure, and the corrected claim does not assert retained foreign-use coverage. The callback gaps (17 readiness, 40 result) all have terminal PASS records, and the note does not count them as passes.\n\nLimits, stated plainly: nothing here reproduces Room A's private confirmed-149 context, so hosted fit at entry 150 and hosted recovery remain unproved until the planner's tail. The note says so.\n\nRollout notes for the planner (nonblocking):\n1. Throughput. Confirmation resets the count, so when every Room A entry refuses adaptively, each entry costs one refused adaptive pass, a short capacity backoff and one fixed pass. That is correct, but it is about twice the passes per entry; watch the rate over the roughly 22,000 remaining entries.\n2. Hard outcomes. The fixed path runs inventory outside lookahead. A debit overrun there, or a null finish quote, returns reason limit and the driver stops the row durably, as the adaptive path already does for its first candidate. Because the retry would repeat the same single entry with a fresh allowance, a stop is an honest result, but in the tail treat state stopped/limit with capacityRefusal site plan-debit as the signal for a restart decision, not a deferral.\n3. Deploy dap-grow with --keep-vars. A deploy from the landed Main also brings dap-grow the BR-1 room file, which is still waiting.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 1d7495bd / tree 4f8f4e61. Builder lands; planner deploys.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8aa9d90cd2b800831a04d8ace85726c5d2075758","binding":"assigned","head":"1d7495bd6a1405a693214b7a2bf9087acae759cf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1688500c7a862bde40ce1478949fd8703e